<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!-- ============================================================================
         CTV v1 BASELINE, part 2 of 2: the CTV domain schema.

         THIS IS THE VERSION 1 BASELINE. Every DCRE database is dropped and recreated
         at the v1 cutover, so this changelog only ever runs against an EMPTY schema.
         That is why the usual re-run guards are absent, and their absence is
         deliberate rather than an oversight:

           - no ANY-checksum override. It existed because an external SQL file was
             edited after it had executed on live databases (A-81). With no recorded
             history there is no checksum to contradict, and suppressing checksum
             validation on a baseline would only disarm the control for every FUTURE
             edit.
           - the three layering columns are declared here rather than added by a
             later ALTER. version / created_at / updated_at arrived in
             2026/07/003-layering.xml as an additive retrofit onto a table that was
             already live. On an empty database the net result is one table with
             eight columns, so that is what this expresses. Carrying the create and
             the ALTER separately would reproduce the retrofit rather than the
             schema.
           - dcre_col.mandate is simply never created. 2026/08/001-drop-local-mandate
             dropped a mandates table that lived in the collections database and that
             no changelog created; in v1 it has no create to undo, so it has no drop
             either. A drop changeset in a baseline is scar tissue: it describes a
             database that no longer exists. CtvManifestParityTest asserts
             information_schema carries no relation named mandate, so the absence is
             tested rather than assumed. The DC-flow mandate gate reads
             dcre_man.man_ctv_view, the contract the mandates family owns.

         ONE guard IS retained, and it is the exception that the rule above is about:
         see the changeset comment. Pure typed tags throughout, no raw-SQL body.

         validation_log is CTV's table: CTV is its only writer (R-04), one row per
         validated detail record, keyed on the arrival and the record sequence.
         ============================================================================ -->

    <changeSet id="ctv-v1-validation-log" author="dcre">
        <!--
          KEPT DELIBERATELY, unlike every other re-run guard in this baseline.

          validation_log CAN already exist on an empty v1 database, so this guard is
          live rather than dead. dcre_col is shared, and CRG mints validation_log as
          a bootstrap read-source when its report window fires before CTV's first
          arrival (crg 001-crg.xml, changeset 001-bootstrap-sources-crg). Which of
          the two reaches Liquibase first is a race decided by pod start order, not
          by anything this changelog controls, so an unguarded createTable here would
          crashloop CTV on exactly the orderings where CRG wins.

          MARK_RAN rather than CONTINUE is correct for THIS dependency, and the
          distinction is the A-79 lesson. CONTINUE is for a dependency that has not
          bootstrapped YET and will exist later, where recording the skip makes it
          permanent. Here the guarded object is the thing this changeset creates: if
          it already exists, the work is genuinely done and will never need doing
          again, so recording it as applied is the truth.

          CRG's DDL is column-for-column identical to the createTable below,
          including the uq_validation_arrival_sequence constraint, so either winner
          leaves the same table.
        -->
        <preConditions onFail="MARK_RAN">
            <not><tableExists tableName="validation_log"/></not>
        </preConditions>

        <createTable tableName="validation_log">
            <column name="id" type="UUID" defaultValueComputed="gen_random_uuid()">
                <constraints primaryKey="true" nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="arrival_id" type="UUID">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="sequence" type="INT">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="outcome" type="VARCHAR(32)">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="detail" type="VARCHAR(256)"/>
            <column name="version" type="BIGINT" defaultValueNumeric="0">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="created_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
            <column name="updated_at" type="TIMESTAMPTZ" defaultValueComputed="now()">
                <constraints nullable="false"/>
            </column>
        </createTable>
        <addUniqueConstraint tableName="validation_log" columnNames="arrival_id, sequence"
                             constraintName="uq_validation_arrival_sequence"/>
        <rollback>
            <dropTable tableName="validation_log"/>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
